      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research low-risk per-state hot-path optimizations: precompute valid neighbor transitions, avoid scanning all boxes for occupancy, update the sorted box-position key incrementally after a push, and skip full key comparisons when stored hashes differ. Retain full state equality checks and use index types that do not truncate valid board positions. Measure the changes separately; the current source’s box scans, sorting, and hash-table lookup are candidates, not confirmed bottlenecks.\",\"B\":\"Research search-space reduction using safe deadlock pruning and a push-oriented state representation keyed by box positions plus the player’s reachable region. Preserve shortest total player-movement length—not merely fewest pushes—by charging walking distances and retaining enough path information to produce the required up, down, left, right lexicographic tie-break. Prove pruning cannot discard a valid optimal solution; compare correctness and explored-state counts against the baseline.\",\"C\":\"Research deterministic parallel expansion of BFS layers on the ARM64 target’s four CPU cores. Preserve shortest-path and tie-break semantics when merging duplicate states and selecting goals; avoid nondeterministic first-writer path selection. The measured baseline is only about 4.75 ms, so test whether parallel overhead is amortized on the available general workload and keep this lane only if end-to-end measurements improve.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only validated programs from A, B, and C. The e1 baseline is correct on 4 cases, with three timings of 0.0046365, 0.0049767, and 0.0046419 seconds (mean 0.0047517 seconds; reported score 0.5); there is no profiler data or evidence that gains compose. Recheck correctness, shortest length, and the official move-order tie-break, then measure individual candidates and the integrated result under the unchanged harness. Do not assume additive gains or retain a combination that regresses performance or correctness.\",\"analysis\":\"The source performs breadth-first state search with sorted box positions, dead-square pruning, chained hash lookup, and per-move box scans. The only automatic run evidence is the correct four-case baseline at roughly 4.75 ms on a four-core ARM64 CPU without a GPU; no hot-path profile is available. The role objectives therefore test distinct hypotheses—state-operation cost, search-space size, and parallelism—while preserving general-input correctness and the official shortest-solution/tie-break requirements.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"efaf4e46b4ea5de9d6d8a2ecb2f3a75fce7698aca3280e158ed2eaef463f6e92\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research low-risk per-state hot-path optimizations: precompute valid neighbor transitions, avoid scanning all boxes for occupancy, update the sorted box-position key incrementally after a push, and skip full key comparisons when stored hashes differ. Retain full state equality checks and use index types that do not truncate valid board positions. Measure the changes separately; the current source’s box scans, sorting, and hash-table lookup are candidates, not confirmed bottlenecks.\",\"B\":\"Research search-space reduction using safe deadlock pruning and a push-oriented state representation keyed by box positions plus the player’s reachable region. Preserve shortest total player-movement length—not merely fewest pushes—by charging walking distances and retaining enough path information to produce the required up, down, left, right lexicographic tie-break. Prove pruning cannot discard a valid optimal solution; compare correctness and explored-state counts against the baseline.\",\"C\":\"Research deterministic parallel expansion of BFS layers on the ARM64 target’s four CPU cores. Preserve shortest-path and tie-break semantics when merging duplicate states and selecting goals; avoid nondeterministic first-writer path selection. The measured baseline is only about 4.75 ms, so test whether parallel overhead is amortized on the available general workload and keep this lane only if end-to-end measurements improve.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only validated programs from A, B, and C. The e1 baseline is correct on 4 cases, with three timings of 0.0046365, 0.0049767, and 0.0046419 seconds (mean 0.0047517 seconds; reported score 0.5); there is no profiler data or evidence that gains compose. Recheck correctness, shortest length, and the official move-order tie-break, then measure individual candidates and the integrated result under the unchanged harness. Do not assume additive gains or retain a combination that regresses performance or correctness.\",\"analysis\":\"The source performs breadth-first state search with sorted box positions, dead-square pruning, chained hash lookup, and per-move box scans. The only automatic run evidence is the correct four-case baseline at roughly 4.75 ms on a four-core ARM64 CPU without a GPU; no hot-path profile is available. The role objectives therefore test distinct hypotheses—state-operation cost, search-space size, and parallelism—while preserving general-input correctness and the official shortest-solution/tie-break requirements.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"c75857faba8440d3baf35f12579472e1\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"efaf4e46b4ea5de9d6d8a2ecb2f3a75fce7698aca3280e158ed2eaef463f6e92\",\"session_id\":\"bb7a58941e74486ba24267f2f526de8f\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"2b49f2926c3c9ccfffa972b6e677c6f175e7612fe6e8c0502e8d16ec79aafdc5\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":13716,\"output_tokens\":4749,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":4250}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":18465,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"comp